    "data_quality_notes": "High quality data with extensive experimental validation. Multiple crystal structures available for armadillo domain and various complexes. Kinetic data for GSK3B interaction well-characterized; less quantitative data available for other interactions. No specific Kd values found for beta-TrCP/phospho-beta-catenin interaction despite its importance. Isoform information limited to canonical sequence; alternative splicing not extensively documented in UniProt.",
    "modeling_relevance_summary": "CTNNB1 is the central node of canonical Wnt signaling, making it critical for pathway modeling. Key for modeling: (1) Sequential phosphorylation by CK1 then GSK3B as priming mechanism, (2) Destruction complex assembly with AXIN as limiting component, (3) Competition between degradation (phosphorylation/ubiquitination) and stabilization (Wnt signaling, acetylation), (4) Nuclear translocation and TCF/LEF binding for transcriptional output, (5) Mutually exclusive binding of adhesion partners (E-cadherin) vs transcriptional partners (TCF/LEF) to same armadillo groove, (6) Multiple positive feedback loops (AXIN2 as Wnt target) and negative regulators (ICAT). Availability of kinetic parameters for GSK3B phosphorylation enables quantitative modeling of destruction complex."
